Z||000000||286SE'S||07-19-2000||05:11 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.pontiworld.com.au/newsletter/july2000/page3.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pontiworld.com.au/newsletter/july2000/page3.html</A> <P>Check out this Austrailian web page it has<BR>a picture of the elusive 1989 FIERO prototype. Page one of the newletter has a picture of a GT that the driver fell asleep in. I hope it was right hand drive! One guy says he spent $25,000 to restore his Fiero.<BR>Are Austrailian dollars like Canada? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||07-19-2000||06:02 PM||||Wow, GREAT find, 286SE's!  It looks like there are two of them - one with the 15" wheels and a wing (GT?) and one with the 14" wheels and a luggage rack (Coupe?).<P>Are these in some obscure GM/Holden junkyard in Australia or something?  I notice all the other cars are GM.  Those chicken-$hits should have the decency to give those cars to the FOCOA museum.  They would cherish them instead of leaving them to rot in a scrapyard halfway around the world.||||reg||14
