Z||000007||ChadMan||07-20-2000||09:18 AM||||So those 89 prototypes are in Detroit?  That makes me feel a little better (nothing against Australia - I just couldn't think of a good reason for GM to send these prototypes Down Under except to "hide" them).  I'm not big on the looks of them, either, but I sure would like a firsthand look at them - wouldn't you?<P>Semi-related topic: remember how the automotive press treated the Fiero?<P>1984:  "It's the greatest thing since sliced bread"<BR>1985:  "It's not so great after all - but the V6 is fun"<BR>1986:  "This car sucks, but the fastback is pretty"<BR>1987:  "This car sucks, period"<BR>1988:  "Oh, GM, how could you discontinue such a great car that everybody loved so much?"||||reg||1
