Z||000021||AusFiero||05-05-2001||09:36 PM||||Sorry to burst ya bubble on this one 286SE'S<BR>but those pictures are the ones I posted a few weeks ago. The cars are not in Australia. I am the guy with over $30,000 tied up in my Fiero. And also a good friend of the owner of Ponti-World, Dave Clee.<BR>To finish the total picture I am also webmaster of all the Ponti-World sites. So I can assure you there are no 1989 Fieros in Australia.<P>See this thread for the fate of the cars in question. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007237.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007237.html</A> <P>And I do have higher resolution shots of the cars available when Dave Clee recoveres from a recent stroke.<P>Here is also the original thread about those cars.http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006649.html||||reg||1
Z||000022||AusFiero||05-05-2001||10:54 PM||||On the blue Fiero. Yep it was right hand drive and the driver survived with minor injuries. There wasn't a lot to be had in the way of parts though. Dave from Ponti-World bought it off the uninsured owner. Almost everything from the rear of the doors back was useable. <P>There wasn't a great deal of room left inside the car. I was quite shocked the guy lived.||||reg||1
Z||000023||AusFiero||05-06-2001||03:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 286SE'S:<BR><B><A HREF="http://www.USGMSERVICEPARTS.COM/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.USGMSERVICEPARTS.COM/</A> <BR>seemed to work o.k. for me. Not much there.It is only good for a laugh unless it is in Austrailian dollars $34.00 PW switch, $57.00 headlight switch and $117.00 door handle!! YIKES!!! lets keep our own Fiero Store.Terry   <BR>[This message has been edited by 286SE'S (edited 07-20-2000).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes some things are expensive 286SE'S but stop to consider the value of the Australian $ at 51c US. Look up more common parts like brake pads and service parts, particularly for the Firebirds. You will see the prices are pretty much the same as American online stores (considering the transport expenses and taxes this end). The trim bits and switches etc are always dear here because they are not bought in bulk. The common parts, well when you buy brake pads at 1000 plus units each time the prices get cheap.<P>From building the site , I know that it has over 1700 Pontiac parts with pictures on it (yes not much Fiero stuff as it really is aimed at the Firebird market until more stock gets put online, it is a big job)and also know from worldwide response to the store that the prices are fair. Ponti-World has customers in the USA (mostly for Ponti-Worlds repros), England, Kuwait, South Africa, New Zealand, Japan and most Asian countries and can still provide parts for competitive prices compared to the American suppliers, due to his buying power with major suppliers and his international shipping experience. A lot of American stores really do have no idea about shipping all over the world fast (not a flame, many do know their shipping, many more don't), that is the reason many buy from Ponti-World instead of America.<P>Basically what it boils down too is Ponti-Worlds stores are aimed at the rest of the world rather than the American market. But Dave, the owner of Ponti-World has been for some time looking into having an American base to ship from to produce a new store priced in American dollars for the American market only. The prices then would be extremely cheap compared to what is currently available to your market as the transport costs and Australian taxes wouldn't be on top of them.<P>Would you's use a USA based store of Ponti-Worlds if you could save 10% to 20% on what you are paying now? I am interested to know as Dave has been considering this for some time now and needs a little push to convince him.<P>Whew, long post but just thought I would let you's know a bit about the idea behind usgmserviceparts.com and Ponti-World in general. <P>I would say direct any questions to Dave at Ponti-World but he is currently recovering from a stroke and isn't up to answering a million questions at present.||||reg||1
